## Start gate

Required completed exports: [Baseline and isolated resumption](Baseline.lingua)

Dependency reason: Every branch must share identity, revisioned source, accepted commands, undo, bounded jobs and artifact persistence before branching.

This is a core work package. Start only after the named providers publish verified native/backend/persistence contracts and the package's implementation scope is authorized. Do not wait for an entire former numbered stage unless that contract acceptance is explicitly listed above. Do not use an unfinished sibling or mocked replacement as a hidden prerequisite.

## Delivered boundary

Native tiny-document create/edit/save/reopen; typed definitions/occurrences, source invalidation, inert behavior selections, local authority, job generations and portable artifact envelope.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Shared nucleus/model, engine acceptance and store schema. One owner of each shared API/migration; no parallel replacement model engines.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 02.T01

- [ ] **02.T01.** Implement definition revisions, stable instance slots/occurrence handles, compact element IDs and optional Record bindings for a tiny repeated scene. Extend existing canonical/asset contracts instead of duplicating identity.

### Task 02.T02

- [ ] **02.T02.** Implement directory save/load, required-profile/closure validation, atomic root publication/recovery and resource bounds. Expose create/open/save, tree/inspector and a revision-conflict flow in native UI. Evaluate compact shared authoring chunks for undo; instrument snapshot pointer/copy/retention costs without allocating an object per future numerical site.

### Task 02.T03

- [ ] **02.T03.** Bridge one existing canvas placement and Room into a model handle; preserve normal selection/undo. Test save failure, crash recovery, repeated definitions, cycle rejection and stale edit results.

### Task 02.T04

- [ ] **02.T04.** Add the minimum shared typed command/receipt, job-generation record and controlled completion/clock boundaries needed by these cases. Prove retry/idempotency and late-result rejection with B20. Instrument admission/queue/commit bytes and latency; defer unused scheduler/database features.

### Task 02.T05

- [ ] **02.T05.** Expose the same typed operation availability, validation, created/changed stable identities and receipt through native controls and the existing authorized programmatic route. Return a minimal source change set and enforce the new modules' dependency boundaries through the existing check tooling; no additional universal command server or whole-application layer rewrite is required. Extend B01/B20/B22 with equivalent outcomes and denied/stale cases. Include Fiote as an Agent client of this same operation path and complete 02.M05 with native UI/result inspection; a generic endpoint alone does not satisfy the Agent workflow.

### Task 02.T08

- [ ] **02.T08.** Complete the first B39 definition-closure/reuse subset with the tiny document: import required permitted definitions, reuse verified identical references, preserve conflicting versions and provenance, and show a simple native imported/reused/unavailable summary. Keep definitions, instance overrides and domain/environment bindings distinct. Do not overwrite an existing shared definition by name or initialize a physical solver; Deferred [stage 16](../contracts/Material-property-contracts.lingua)/[stage 18](../contracts/Rigid-and-articulated-physics-contracts.lingua) add actual material/gravity behavior to the same contract after their own verified providers; preserve existing implemented behavior and passive definitions independently.

### Task 02.T11

- [ ] **02.T11.** Deliver the minimal behavior definition/selection contract below using two real B42 input descriptors, native tree/inspector controls and the existing typed command/save path. Validate references, bounded payloads and source invalidation; do not implement the stage 07 evaluator or a speculative registry of every scientific domain.

